# 10. Success Criteria

## Purpose

The Success Criteria define the measurable conditions by which the progress and overall success of the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) project shall be evaluated.

These criteria provide objective benchmarks to assess whether the project is fulfilling its intended purpose and advancing according to its engineering objectives.

---

## Success Criteria

### SC-001 — Engineering Foundation

A complete and governed engineering repository shall be established and maintained throughout the lifecycle of the project.

---

### SC-002 — Engineering Documentation

Core engineering documents, including the Project Charter, System Objective Specification (SOS), System Requirements Specification (SRS), and supporting engineering architectures, shall be completed, reviewed, approved, and maintained.

---

### SC-003 — Traceability

Engineering objectives, requirements, architectures, analyses, and validation activities shall remain fully traceable throughout the project lifecycle.

---

### SC-004 — Engineering Validation

Engineering concepts and proposed system solutions shall be evaluated through scientific analysis, mathematical modelling, simulation, testing, and engineering review where applicable.

---

### SC-005 — Engineering Consistency

All engineering activities shall remain aligned with the approved engineering philosophy, governance framework, and project objectives.

---

### SC-006 — Knowledge Preservation

Engineering knowledge generated during the project shall be preserved within the governed engineering repository to support future development, collaboration, and continuous improvement.

---

### SC-007 — Project Evolution

The project shall demonstrate the ability to evolve through controlled engineering change while preserving repository integrity, document traceability, and engineering consistency.
